    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The drama of this dish is in the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "tableside-cooking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "tableside cooking "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "yunnan-broth"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Yunnan broth"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " must be at a rolling boil when it hits the bowl. Diners add the raw chicken slices first, then vegetables, then the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "rice-vermicelli"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "rice noodles"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " last. Everything cooks in minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The broth is the foundation. Spend time building it properly. A watery broth makes this dish worthless. The chicken slices must be extremely thin, almost translucent, so they cook through quickly in the hot broth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
